        ":question/id": "d57eb0df-b672-57ca-8fc9-d0cc8d741df8",
        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ for $f(x)={x}^{5}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}.$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The function $f(x)$  is the sum of two power functions. So, we apply the sum rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4/3}) \\\\  & =5{x}^{(5-1)}+\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{(4/3-1)} \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}+\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{1/3} \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt[3]{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
